  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 35 actions (src/actions.js, all registered in one setActionDefinitions call) and 9 boolean feedbacks (src/feedbacks.js). Nothing is generated at runtime.",
    "Protocol: OSC over UDP. The module sends to the configured target host and send port (default 7401) and listens on the receive port (default 7400, bound to 0.0.0.0); src/main.js getConfigFields, src/osc_server.js. Disguise has to be set up to send OSC feedback (companion/HELP.md: full functionality only if Disguise is configured to always send OSC feedback).",
    "Most fields are text inputs with useVariables. Several numeric text inputs declare min/max/step in the source; Companion does not enforce limits on text inputs and the module does not clamp them (only the brightness and volume step actions clamp the resulting value to 0.0-1.0 in src/utils.js), so these bounds appear only in the option description. The regular expressions are recorded as written in the source; each numeric one also accepts a $(variable) reference.",
    "Defaults of text inputs are partly numbers in the source (for example default 1 on the cue and trackid actions); they are recorded unchanged.",
    "shift, shift_brightness and shift_volume use a module-internal shift flag (src/utils.js) that the shift action toggles. The brightness and volume step actions compute the new value from the variables \"brightness\" and \"volume\", which are filled from OSC messages received from Disguise.",
    "layer_speed sends an OSC float argument built with parseInt, so only whole numbers are sent (src/actions.js:669-670). Layer actions build the path from the base address (default /d3/layer/), the layer name and a fixed suffix, for example /d3/layer/<layer>/tint.r.",
    "custom_osc sends any path starting with \"/\" with one string, integer or float argument, integer parts such as 1.2.5 as several integer arguments, or no argument; the value field is only shown when the argument type is not \"none\". It can address anything Disguise accepts.",
    "The feedbacks PlayMode, Heartbeat, Brightness and Volume depend on a 500 ms blink timer (src/main.js) and on variables from received OSC; custom_osc_feedback compares the last received first argument for an OSC path with an expected value (equals, contains or regex). Variables (heartbeat, trackposition_*, timecodeposition_*, trackname, trackid, section names and times, volume, brightness, bpm, playMode) are defined in src/variables.js and are not catalogued.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.15.0: options do not support expressions."
  ]
}
